(* expect:
ignored 0
open 0
restarted 0
ended 1
done
*)
(* #165 D2/D6, rete#312: the WHOLE chain, on host — a `profile <ms>` line (the
   cable's and the debugger's spelling; rete#415 made porta's a goal/profile cell,
   10_profile_cell) -> the kernel's Profiler (installed by the Supervisor before this main: runs) -> its timer ->
   `sys/profileEnd`. 02_dbg_req_profile covers only `parseProfileMs:`, a pure
   function.

   Since rete#312 this drives the REAL handler, not a reproduced body: the app
   only dispatches `sys/timer` (which is all a reactor node does) and counts the
   `sys/profileEnd` events beside the kernel's own reaction. Delete the
   Supervisor's `install:` or the Profiler's wiring and `open`/`ended` go wrong.
   Leg 8 of `nodus/oevm/tests/porta_sync_host.sh` is the gate for the bridge's
   half (a real `porta put` of goal/profile over UDP).

   The build under test has no OEVM_METHOD_PROFILE, so `profileStart`/
   `profileStop` are no-ops (01_window_lifecycle): the COUNTS are a C unit test
   (test_mprof_gate); what this file gates is the WIRING, on the host virtual
   clock — never wall time, so the sequence is exact.

   `restarted 0` is the load-bearing line. Without the cancel in
   Profiler>>open: the first window's end-timer survives the restart, fires at
   its own deadline, and closes the second window early — the line would read
   `restarted 1`. *)
class DbgReqChainTest packageUsing: manifest = (
  | private ends ::= 0. |
) (
  public main: platform args: args = (
    | space timers prof |
    space:: platform space.
    timers:: platform timers.     (* the kernel's one instance — the Profiler's too *)
    space whenever: 'sys/timer' do: [ :e | timers dispatch: e ].
    (space channel: 'sys/profileEnd') whenever: '' do: [ :m | self ended ].
    prof:: platform profiler.

    (* A line naming no duration must arm NOTHING. *)
    prof request: 'reboot now'. space drain.
    platform advanceMillis: 1000. space drain.
    ('ignored ' , ends printString) println.

    (* clock 1000: a 100 ms window opens, due at 1100 *)
    prof request: 'profile 100'. space drain.
    platform advanceMillis: 50. space drain.          (* clock 1050, not due *)
    ('open ' , ends printString) println.

    (* clock 1050: a start while the window is open RESTARTS it — the 1100
       timer is cancelled and a 200 ms one is armed, due at 1250. *)
    prof request: 'profile 200'. space drain.
    platform advanceMillis: 60. space drain.          (* clock 1110, PAST 1100 *)
    ('restarted ' , ends printString) println.

    platform advanceMillis: 200. space drain.         (* clock 1310, past 1250 *)
    ('ended ' , ends printString) println.
    'done' println.
    ^ 0 )

  ended = ( ends:: ends + 1. ^ self )
) : (
)
